 "world_update": {
 "context": "Enrollment continues steadily with slight growth at Sites A and B and first screenings initiated at Site C; protocol visit windows and regional targets remain unchanged. A routine internal memo from the sponsor reiterates that all protocol visits should follow the defined windows and that lab collection dates, not order dates, should be used as the primary reference for lab timing across the program.",
 "resource": "Core staffing levels remain tight but adequate; Site B’s coordinator reports needing to defer some non‑urgent query resolution to focus on upcoming visits. The dashboards now show improved completeness for recruitment source fields but still indicate a handful of missing outreach‑note entries at Site C, where data entry is slightly delayed.",
 "actors": "Site A’s team gains confidence in checking visit windows directly in the protocol and is less likely to ask about clearly in‑window dates. Site B’s coordinator standardizes their revised screening checklist and shares it internally with the investigator for sign‑off. At Site C, the coordinator begins scheduling their first Week 4 visits and notices that one requested participant date would land slightly later than most prior examples, prompting a question about the outer limit of the window."
 },
 "antecedent": "Site C seeks clarification on whether a proposed Week 4 visit date is still acceptable within the allowed window and asks for confirmation on how to handle recruitment‑source and outreach‑note fields for their first participants.",
 "perceived_simulation": "[Messages]\n[system-dashboard]: Current regional dashboard: Site A has 3 screened and 2 enrolled participants; Site B has 2 screened and 1 enrolled; Site C has just screened its first participant. All required safety assessments remain on time. Recruitment-source fields are now complete for most records, though Site C shows missing outreach‑notes for its initial screenings.\n[Site_C_Coordinator]: \"Hi. We have our first participant approaching the Week 4 visit. Based on their availability, the only realistic slot is on Day 30. The protocol describes a Week 4 window but does not explicitly mention Day 30 in the examples. Can you confirm whether Day 30 is still within the acceptable window, or should we push harder for an earlier day? Also, for our first few participants, could you confirm what level of detail you expect us to enter in the recruitment‑source and outreach‑notes fields so we’re consistent with the rest of the region?\"\n[Sponsor_Operations_Lead]: \"Thanks for helping standardize the use of lab collection dates and recruitment documentation. We haven’t changed any visit windows, so please continue to rely on the written protocol and EDC guidance. Let us know if a site faces a genuinely borderline scheduling case that might fall outside the defined windows so we can review it together.\"",
 "response": "I can’t confirm Day 30 without checking the written protocol window; please first verify whether Week‑4 explicitly includes Day 30 — if it does, book the visit, but if it’s ambiguous or outside the window and you cannot rebook earlier, send me the de‑identified participant code plus the proposed Day‑30 appointment and I will escalate to the sponsor for review. \nFor outreach‑notes, use a consistent template: recruitment_source (category + brief origin), outreach_date/time, contact_method, contact_person, succinct summary of the discussion (eligibility questions, barriers), screening outcome, and planned next steps. \nRemember to enter lab collection dates (not order dates) into the EDC and complete the missing outreach‑notes for your initial screenings today. \nAfter you confirm the Day‑30 check or send the de‑identified escalation packet, update me and I’ll coordinate with Sponsor Operations if needed."
 },
 {
