 },
 "antecedent": "Coordinators from Sites A and C, along with Site B’s investigator, seek your guidance on how to roll out the clarified Week 8 safety-assessment documentation in a way that stays consistent across the region without overloading already stretched staff or disrupting upcoming Week 8 scheduling.",
 "perceived_simulation": "[Messages]\n[system-dashboard]: \"Updated regional metrics: Site A has 7 enrolled participants, Site B has 4 enrolled and 2 screened, and Site C has 4 enrolled. The Week 8 visit calendar shows that one of the previously busiest lab days now has moderate capacity after rescheduling, while several later days remain lightly booked. Safety assessments are recorded at all required time points so far, with no high-grade adverse events pending review.\"\n[Sponsor_Operations_Lead]: \"We’ve issued a clarification on the [safety assessment]: going forward, it must be documented at screening and all Week 8 visits in a way that clearly separates the two defined subcomponents, while still mapping to the existing eCRF fields. No new items are being added, but the layout should make it obvious that both subcomponents were completed. The template Site B shared appears compatible with this, if it is adjusted to show both pieces explicitly. Please help your sites adopt a consistent approach without delaying required visits.\"\n[Site_A_Coordinator]: \"Hello. We’ve been using our original safety-assessment notes so far and are open to switching to a standardized layout for Week 8 now that the clarification is out. We have several Week 8 visits coming up over the next three weeks. How would you recommend we transition—should we switch immediately for all upcoming Week 8 visits, or phase it in after a brief training so we don’t risk confusion at the visits already scheduled?\"\n[Site_B_Investigator]: \"Good afternoon. Our revised [safety assessment] template already separates the two subcomponents, but we want to be sure it fully satisfies the sponsor’s new clarification at both screening and Week 8. Would you like us to adjust this template further and share a ‘regional version’ with the other sites, or is it better for each site to adapt their own documentation as long as the subcomponents are clearly visible and mapped to the eCRF?\"\n[Site_C_Coordinator]: \"Hi. With the staffing we have, I’m worried about taking on too many documentation changes at once. We can keep doing what we’ve been doing for the next few weeks, but we don’t want to end up having to redo notes later if the region standardizes on something else. Could you advise whether we should wait for a common template to be finalized for Week 8 safety assessments, or go ahead and make local adjustments now?\"",
 "response": "Decision: we will adopt a single regional screening/Week‑8 layout using Site B’s template as the base, adjusted to label the two required subcomponents explicitly and accompanied by a one‑page field‑mapping to the eCRF. \nSite B — please finalize the adjusted template, upload it to the shared folder, and email the sponsor operations lead with the mapping within 24 hours so I can circulate the regional version to Sites A and C. \nAll sites — attend a required 30‑minute virtual training I’ll schedule within 48 hours and then implement the regional template for all upcoming Week‑8 visits immediately; if you cannot attend, implement within 72 hours and until then ensure both subcomponents are clearly documented in source notes and mapped to the eCRF so no rework will be needed. \nDo not change or redo prior visit source records; add a brief dated addendum only if a prior record lacks explicit separation and re‑entry would be required. \nIf any site cannot meet these timelines or needs a fillable PDF/quick‑start sheet, notify me within 24 hours and I will provide the regional file and guide."
 },
