 "antecedent": "As the first Week 8 visits using the new regional template approach, coordinators from two sites raise questions about exactly when to switch templates and how to handle participants who have screening documented in the old layout but upcoming Week 8 visits under the new one.",
 "perceived_simulation": "[Messages]\n[system-dashboard]: \"Updated regional metrics: Site A has 8 enrolled participants, Site B has 5 enrolled and 2 screened, and Site C has 5 enrolled. Several Week 8 visits are scheduled over the next three weeks, with lab capacity appearing balanced after prior adjustments. Safety assessments are documented at all required time points, though the format varies by site pending full rollout of the new regional template. No high-grade adverse events are pending review.\"\n[Sponsor_Operations_Lead]: \"We’ve reviewed the regional safety-assessment template and mapping you circulated. It looks aligned with our clarification as long as both subcomponents are always completed and clearly labeled at screening and Week 8. Please confirm that all sites have a clear go-live date and that the new layout will not delay scheduled visits. Do not ask sites to rewrite past notes—add clarifying addenda only if absolutely necessary.\"\n[Site_A_Coordinator]: \"Hello. We have our first Week 8 visits using the new safety-assessment layout coming up early next week. Our screening visits for these participants were documented with our original format. Can you confirm whether it is acceptable for screening to be in the old layout and Week 8 to be in the new regional template for the same participant, as long as both subcomponents are clearly documented at each time point? Also, should we start using the new layout for any remaining screening visits now, or only for Week 8?\"\n[Site_C_Coordinator]: \"Hi. We’re ready in principle to adopt the regional safety-assessment template, but with our current staffing we’re worried about having to redo anything later. For participants who have already completed screening using our old notes and will have Week 8 in a few weeks, do you recommend we add a brief addendum to the old screening notes to explicitly label the two subcomponents, or is it sufficient to leave screening as is and only use the regional template going forward? We’d appreciate precise instructions so we don’t create extra work or inconsistencies across the region.\"",
 "response": "Yes — it is acceptable for a participant’s screening to remain in the old site‑specific layout while Week‑8 uses the new regional template, provided that at each visit both required subcomponents are explicitly documented and mapped to the eCRF. Do not rewrite prior source notes; add a brief dated addendum only if a prior screening record does not clearly show both subcomponents (flag any such records to me and I will advise whether an addendum is required). Effective immediately the regional template is the go‑live for all upcoming Week‑8 visits and for any new screening visits going forward; if any site anticipates this change will delay a scheduled visit, notify me within 24 hours so we can coordinate alternatives. Please email confirmation within 24 hours that you will follow this approach and list any screening records you think may need addenda."
 }
